{"id": "EUVD-2026-64538", "enisaUuid": "df9ae4ef-2d5d-315c-836c-c7e69e1c6bfc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nring-buffer: Use current_context for safe per-CPU buffer swap\n\nThe ring_buffer_swap_cpu() function currently checks the per-CPU\ncommitting counter to determine if a buffer is actively being written to\nbefore performing the swap. However, there exists a race window where\nthis check can be bypassed:\n\n    ring_buffer_lock_reserve\n        cpu_buffer = buffer->buffers[cpu];       // cpu_buffer_a\n        rb_reserve_next_event\n            rb_start_commit // inc committing\n            if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(cpu_buffer->buffer) != buffer)) {...}\n            __rb_reserve_next\n                rb_move_tail\n                    rb_end_commit(cpu_buffer);   // dec committing => 0\n                    /* interrupt hits here, successfully swaps! */\n                    local_inc(&cpu_buffer->committing);\n\n    ring_buffer_unlock_commit\n        cpu_buffer = buffer->buffers[cpu];      // cpu_buffer_b\n        rb_commit\n            rb_end_commit\n            RB_WARN_ON(cpu_buffer, !local_read(&cpu_buffer->committing))\n                                                // triggers warning\n\nThe committing counter can temporarily drop to 0 during a single write\noperation (within rb_move_tail), creating a window where swap can\nsucceed even though the write is still in progress. This leads to\ninconsistent buffer state and triggers the RB_WARN_ON in rb_commit().\n\nReplace the committing counter check with current_context checks, which\nare set at the entry of ring_buffer_lock_reserve() and remain valid\nthroughout the entire write operation, providing a reliable indicator of\nbuffer busy state during swap.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:31:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:06:00", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26662bc8fced1d668fa1aa146eda085bfc67bd0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b524e6b234e45c7f5f90d13b042c6f57f80105c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/597f279b7b4a06412e3d965e98cc36e181cdbede", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22709117d9ae95e52673685f98caac7c356a8227", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad7e10c7ea89af45ac1bf1814855d45da472703d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b926fb04cb9ef3156dcf88c69a59d3d1a1c4f9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e6e2a18c20e88167d414f666032792e8bf19b80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f27bdc43077e4fcb5557dfc315ee8d91e741f483"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j5v7-fqrf-q39x", "CVE-2026-74601"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c16ff56-e673-3f35-a067-dc3807ff2582", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.217"}, {"id": "0fadf6c9-2219-31ed-a262-860caf8a0431", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.105"}, {"id": "29aae0bd-7917-3ecb-b952-d5081884ce14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <5b926fb04cb9ef3156dcf88c69a59d3d1a1c4f9f"}, {"id": "3d7c06e9-1fd9-3f45-ab73-10e704c78d49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "472c523d-35cd-33c0-aaa0-bb1bc99f67a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <5e6e2a18c20e88167d414f666032792e8bf19b80"}, {"id": "4c062e08-4854-36d4-b8d2-7d6c7f697f7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "5004c9f2-53a3-3f72-9b0a-73b5bc9c5185", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <ad7e10c7ea89af45ac1bf1814855d45da472703d"}, {"id": "5d989c51-f3ed-38ec-ad07-d234c223bc7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <597f279b7b4a06412e3d965e98cc36e181cdbede"}, {"id": "6a40aec6-672d-3757-90af-58ac686dac22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.153"}, {"id": "6a9c8434-84b0-3ffe-a8b0-4b68bc64e398", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <f27bdc43077e4fcb5557dfc315ee8d91e741f483"}, {"id": "7abd4ec1-4231-3e44-a2f4-3508a10a68ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <22709117d9ae95e52673685f98caac7c356a8227"}, {"id": "84297729-1439-378d-9ce2-09fe10cbf96f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.5"}, {"id": "a4f60db2-83ad-35fa-ac8c-33c3d3b0af25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.266"}, {"id": "a5daeb18-815a-3b80-b1d9-2885f1420bdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a8bf7831-4d10-3d2a-b41e-5354b353f28c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "c656939d-6438-3432-90bb-4ef966da1712", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.184"}, {"id": "df60c31f-95af-3887-8308-e9a159761b86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <6b524e6b234e45c7f5f90d13b042c6f57f80105c"}, {"id": "eb10a7d3-2a9e-3be5-8e86-d472180203b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4239c38fe0b3847e1e6d962c74b41b08ba0e2990 <26662bc8fced1d668fa1aa146eda085bfc67bd0b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "422cfb33-14e9-31d0-a3f3-24a0283ddea8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}